  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#keys"/>
    <title type="link" role="trail">Babble Help</title>
    <title type="text">Keyboard</title>
    <title type="link">Keyboard</title>
    <desc>The shortcuts that work anywhere in Babble.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Keyboard</title>

  <p>
    <link xref="desktop">Ctrl+,</link> opens Preferences, <link xref="settings">Ctrl+1</link>
    through <link xref="settings">Ctrl+9</link> jump between places,
    <link xref="settings">Alt+Left</link> goes back and <link xref="settings">Ctrl+R</link>
    reloads. Press <key>F1</key> for this help, or <key>Ctrl+?</key> to list
    every shortcut.
  </p>
  <p>
    While a page in the web column has the focus, <key>Ctrl+R</key> and
    <key>F5</key> reload the page, <key>Alt+Left</key> and <key>Alt+Right</key>
    go back and forward, and <key>Escape</key> or <key>Ctrl+W</key> hides
    the column.
  </p>

  <section id="shortcuts">
    <title>Every shortcut</title>
    <p>
      The full list opens with <key>Ctrl+?</key>. What follows are the ones
      that work from anywhere in the window.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item><key>Ctrl+N</key> opens the composer</item>
      <item><key>Ctrl+F</key> searches</item>
      <item><key>Ctrl+R</key> reloads the timeline</item>
      <item><key>Ctrl+1</key>–<key>Ctrl+9</key> jump between sidebar places</item>
      <item><key>Alt+Left</key> goes back, <key>Alt+Right</key> forward</item>
      <item><key>Ctrl+,</key> opens Preferences</item>
      <item><key>F1</key> opens this help</item>
      <item><key>Ctrl+?</key> lists every shortcut</item>
    </list>
  </section>

</page>